From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 08:53:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: tpg: set the media entity function

The test pattern generator sub-devices are registered without a media
entity function, so the media core warns for each of them at probe:

  qcom-camss 9253000.isp: Entity type for entity msm_tpg0 was not initialized!

Give them the function the other CAMSS sub-devices (CSIPHY, CSID, ISPIF,
VFE) use, MEDIA_ENT_F_PROC_VIDEO_PIXEL_FORMATTER. MEDIA_ENT_F_CAM_SENSOR
is not used: camss_find_sensor_pad() would then take a TPG for an image
sensor and ask it for a link frequency, and libcamera's simple pipeline
handler would try to create a camera for every TPG.

Fixes: 70b193987c8c ("media: qcom: camss: Add common TPG support")
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-tpg.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-tpg.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-tpg.c
index 5764a60fa34c..9b66eb04afe1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-tpg.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-tpg.c
@@ -490,6 +490,7 @@ int msm_tpg_register_entity(struct tpg_device *tpg,
 
 	tpg->pad.flags = MEDIA_PAD_FL_SOURCE;
 
+	sd->entity.function = MEDIA_ENT_F_PROC_VIDEO_PIXEL_FORMATTER;
 	sd->entity.ops = &tpg_media_ops;
 	ret = media_entity_pads_init(&sd->entity, 1, &tpg->pad);
 	if (ret < 0) {
